@startuml InquiryPermission

title Inquiry Permission API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Inquiry Permission Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_permission" as m_permission
    database "t_permission_scope" as t_permission_scope
    database "m_scope" as m_scope
end box

user -> page: Read permissions and scope definitions with optional filters and pagination
activate page
    page -> api: GET v1/author/permission (Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp; query only)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**InquiryPermissionQueryHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate query/header/body and checked pagination (400) -> verify JWT/roles (401) -> begin
                read-only repeatable-read transaction -> fresh now/expiry -> joined current credential/user (401) -> claims
                permission (403) -> count -> optional page -> optional page-only definitions -> optional exact masters ->
                complete nested mapping -> COMMIT -> 200. Every post-BEGIN rejection rolls back.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate UTC timestamp, known single query keys/no body, UUID id, positive signed Int64 pages/default 1/10/pageSize <=100 and ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED filter
            note over app, infra
                Reject unknown/repeated keys and malformed header/query with 400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId if
                omitted. Supplied id is a non-empty UUID, never null; omitted id is typed SQL NULL. pageIndex/pageSize are
                positive signed 64-bit integers, default 1/10 only when omitted, pageSize at most 100. Compute checked
                offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize and reject parse/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT with 400.
                Explicit empty/null-like values do not become defaults. Row status must be one of ACTIVE, INACTIVE, LOCKED,
                ARCHIVED.
                Validate result sets before mapping: parent ids are unique; each definition belongs to a returned page
                permission, has a unique permission_scope_id and a unique scope_id within that parent, and is not DELETED.
                Each requested master id appears exactly once and every definition resolves to its exact master. Reject
                out-of-set/duplicate/missing/null/malformed required results as internal 500, never omit an unresolved link
                or return a partial catalog. Database foreign keys normally guarantee references, but mapping failures still
                roll back.
            end note
            app -> app: Compute checked offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize; reject numeric/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT
            alt Invalid input or pagination overflow
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                    page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim as unique non-empty strings
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                    page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
            app -> app: Bind omitted id/searchPattern/rowStatus as typed SQL NULL; supplied searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving ILIKE wildcards
            app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
            note over app, infra
                Verify Bearer JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim before BEGIN. roles must be an array of unique non-empty role names (JWT payload of 2026-11-13), including [].
                Missing/malformed roles is generic 401 E10002, never an empty-list or live-grant fallback. Derive
                callerUserId only from verified sub and accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact JWT; do not accept caller
                ids or isPlatformAdmin flags from requests.
                Require matching token hash/caller id, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now;
                missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched credentials is generic 401 E10002 with rollback before
                permission reads. No user/permission/scope/token locks or writes. This current credential gate preserves
                logout/reset revocation (Q13): changes committed before its snapshot are observed. A concurrent revocation
                after the read snapshot starts is not serialized by this read-only inquiry; no credential lock or second
                snapshot is claimed.
                Credential/count/page/definition/master SELECTs share the same read-only repeatable-read snapshot.
                Concurrent permission/link/master insert, rename, status change or removal cannot produce mixed versions
                within this response; the next inquiry sees committed changes. No locks, extra snapshots or writes are
                introduced.
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Read and mapping work completes
                note over app, infra
                    Credentials, count, page, definitions and masters use one read-only repeatable-read snapshot.
                    No locks or writes; do not serialize an in-flight read against revocation after its snapshot.
                    Timeout or unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure may interrupt any step; no partial response.
                end note
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before joined credential read; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired before fresh credential read
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                        page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                        page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload current grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to read permissions.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                        page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get total items
                infra -> m_permission: QUERY - Get total items
                activate m_permission
                    note right of m_permission
                        SELECT
                            COUNT(p.id) as total_items
                        FROM author.m_permission p
                        WHERE p.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR p.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR p.name ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR p.description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR p.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                    end note
                    m_permission -> infra: Return totalItems for non-DELETED permissions and all nullable filters
                deactivate m_permission
                infra -> app: Return totalItems for non-DELETED permissions and all nullable filters
                app -> app: totalPages = 0 when totalItems=0, otherwise integer quotient plus nonzero remainder; no floating point or overflowing count+pageSize-1
                alt totalItems = 0
                    app -> app: items = []; skip page/definition/master queries; totalPages = 0
                else totalItems > 0
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get permissions
                    infra -> m_permission: QUERY - Get permissions
                    activate m_permission
                        note right of m_permission
                            SELECT
                                p.id as permission_id,
                                p.name,
                                p.description,
                                p.row_status
                            FROM author.m_permission p
                            WHERE p.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR p.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR p.name ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR p.description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR p.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                            ORDER BY p.name, p.id
                            LIMIT '<sequence.pageSize>' OFFSET '<sequence.offset>'
                        end note
                        m_permission -> infra: Return four parent columns in name/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    deactivate m_permission
                    infra -> app: Return four parent columns in name/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    app -> app: Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); unique parent UUIDs and non-null required columns; mismatch is internal failure
                    alt Page contains rows
                        app -> app: Bind permissionIds as distinct typed UUID[] from returned page permission_id values only; never request ids or all unpaged matches
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Get the scopes of the permissions
                        infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Get the scopes of the permissions
                        activate t_permission_scope
                            note right of t_permission_scope
                                SELECT
                                    ps.id as permission_scope_id,
                                    ps.permission_id,
                                    ps.scope_id,
                                    ps.row_status
                                FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                                WHERE ps.permission_id = ANY ('<sequence.permissionIds>'::UUID[])
                                AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                ORDER BY ps.permission_id, ps.id
                            end note
                            t_permission_scope -> infra: Return non-DELETED definitions for page parents only, including inactive/locked/archived definitions
                        deactivate t_permission_scope
                        infra -> app: Return non-DELETED definitions for page parents only, including inactive/locked/archived definitions
                        app -> app: Validate definition ids/parent membership/unique scopeId per parent/non-DELETED status and non-null required columns
                        alt Definition rows exist
                            app -> app: Bind scopeIds as distinct typed UUID[] from returned definition scope_id values
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Get scope
                            infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Get scope
                            activate m_scope
                                note right of m_scope
                                    SELECT
                                        s.id as scope_id,
                                        s.scope,
                                        s.name
                                    FROM author.m_scope s
                                    WHERE s.id = ANY ('<sequence.scopeIds>'::UUID[])
                                    ORDER BY s.scope, s.id
                                end note
                                m_scope -> infra: Return exact referenced master scope_id/scope/name in database scope-code/id order, all lifecycle statuses
                            deactivate m_scope
                            infra -> app: Return exact referenced master scope_id/scope/name in database scope-code/id order, all lifecycle statuses
                            app -> app: Require one exact master for every referenced scope_id, no duplicate/out-of-set/missing/null results; failure is internal 500, never silently drop a definition
                            app -> app: Build master rank from database scope-code/id order; preserve closed-master metadata and exact scope_id identity, never rebind by reused code
                            app -> app: Prepare groups by permission_id, ordered by master rank then definition UUID; definition rowStatus is separate from master status
                        else No definition rows
                            app -> app: Set all page scopes=[]; skip master query
                        end
                        loop Map every returned permission in page order
                            app -> app: Map exactly permissionId/name/description/scopes/rowStatus; scopes is [] when no owned definitions; exclude caller/assignment/token/hash/audit
                            loop Map every owned definition in master-rank/id order
                                app -> app: Map exactly permissionScopeId/scopeId/scope/scopeName/rowStatus from definition plus exact master; rowStatus comes from definition; preserve stored metadata
                            end
                        end
                    else Page beyond range contains no rows
                        app -> app: items = []; retain positive totalItems/totalPages; skip definition/master queries; no 404
                    end
                end
                app -> app: data = exactly items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages; echo validated page values; explicit empty arrays; finish full nested mapping
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed consistent read-only permission catalog
                note over app, infra
                    Approved by the product owner (A12); use exact PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT role claims under
                    [owner-confirmed review](../../../../../docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-07-api-review-design.md),
                    Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13. This detailed revision remains in-review; no backend/schema implementation.
                    Omitted searchPattern binds typed SQL NULL; supplied search, including empty string, becomes one bound text
                    searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving percent/underscore wildcards. Never interpolate
                    client text into SQL. The three nullable filters disable only themselves and combine by AND; id is still
                    filtered/paginated, not an unpaged alternate path.
                    After current credentials pass, authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT
                    roles. Valid roles=[] or any other role name is 403 E10009 `You do not have permission to read permissions.`
                    after rollback and before count/page SQL. Never query current caller role assignments to grant, remove or
                    replace authorization. Grant withdrawal after token issuance leaves the old privilege usable until access
                    expiry (Q4); refresh reloads current grants (Q7). Permission catalog metadata returned below comes from the
                    database snapshot, distinct from author/me's calling-token snapshot.
                    Count first and optionally fetch the page in the same read-only repeatable-read snapshot as credentials.
                    Both permission queries use identical non-DELETED/id/searchPattern/rowStatus WHERE predicates; every
                    supplied value is bound, including pageSize and checked offset. If totalItems=0 skip the page SQL and return
                    items=[], totalPages=0. With positive count, query the requested page; an offset beyond the range returns
                    items=[] with positive totals/pages and no 404. A missing/DELETED id is the same empty-list 200 for an
                    authorized caller; permission is checked before revealing whether any permission exists.
                    Permissions with rowStatus DELETED are never returned. Omitted rowStatus preserves every non-DELETED status;
                    supplied status accepts only ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED. Sort by name then id ascending, preserving
                    database collation. This is deterministic within one snapshot; later requests may see newly committed
                    changes and are not a frozen paging cursor.
                    Map each row to exactly permissionId/name/description/scopes/rowStatus. The scopes property is always an
                    array. No caller id, assignment, token/hash, audit or extra table fields are returned. Return exactly five
                    data keys: items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages, with explicit empty arrays. Echo validated pages
                    and compute totalPages by integer quotient/remainder (zero when count=0), avoiding floating point or
                    overflowing count+pageSize-1. Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch or
                    malformed/null/missing required data is internal failure.
                    After a populated page, bind permissionIds as the distinct UUID[] of that page's returned permission_id
                    values only. Fetch non-DELETED permission-scope definitions in one query, including
                    ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED definitions; do not filter by master status or caller grants. Never query
                    definitions from request ids or all matching unpaged parents. An empty page skips both definition and master
                    queries. A page with no definitions maps scopes=[] for every item and skips the master query. No
                    per-permission or per-scope SQL queries.
                    If definitions exist, bind scopeIds as their distinct UUID[] and fetch the exact referenced masters,
                    including INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED/DELETED masters. Preserve this existing administrative catalog behavior:
                    closed-master metadata remains available for Q23 cleanup. It is distinct from ACTIVE-only login/refresh
                    claim eligibility. Metadata is matched by immutable scope_id, never by a potentially reused scope code. No
                    added master-status response field and no implicit answer that these catalog scopes are granted to the
                    caller.
                    Map every definition to exactly permissionScopeId/scopeId/scope/scopeName/rowStatus, using definition
                    id/scope_id/row_status plus the matching master scope/name. The returned rowStatus is the definition's
                    status, not the master's. Preserve non-null string metadata as stored; do not rewrite legacy values. Order
                    each parent's scopes by database scope-code collation, then master id, then definition id: derive master
                    rank from the master query's ORDER BY scope,id and order each parent's links by that rank and definition
                    UUID. Keep parent page order independent from the global master order. Preserve empty scopes arrays and all
                    five fields of each nested object.
                    Map the full response before COMMIT, then HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Permission Success. An unexpected
                    SQL/result/mapping error rolls back and returns generic 500 without bizCode; timeout before COMMIT rolls
                    back and returns 408 E90001. Never return partially mapped rows, mutate
                    permissions/definitions/masters/assignments/tokens/audit, or answer 404/409 for this inquiry.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Permission Success; all five pagination keys
                api -> page: Show authorized permission catalog and totals
                page -> user: Display permissions with scopes or empty page
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial permission catalog
                page -> user: Display failure; no permission data
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
